# Context

## Background
The owner pushed menubar-session-tags (b7e31f1 and fbce579) on
2026-11-25 and asked "review work i did and merge it if ok". v0.8.0
was cut first, because the release was requested first and this VM
cannot build the Swift app.

## Review
No blocker. An independent review agent reported seven findings and
each one was checked against the code. None changes the merge:
- On a paired device the uploader stores sessions under the device ID
  of credential.json, while the new topology.device_id reads
  device.json. The two are equal after a normal join. They differ
  only after device.json is recreated, a state that existed before
  this branch. The menu bar app then labels the sessions of this Mac
  as those of another device. No check reports that state today.
- docs/reference.md says that the status output carries this device's
  ID. Only the JSON output does.
- The hub device ID of the diagnostics frame is the identity of
  ohya serve. It equals the identity of ohya ingest only when both
  use one state directory, which ohya setup --hub guarantees.
- status grades an unusable device.json as warn and doctor as error.
  The exit code of status is the same for both.
- The Hub reachable row copies the layout of row(_:value:), and the
  dot color is repeated in two places.
- VoiceOver reads the name of the symbol of a tag before its text.
- The two commit subjects have 57 and 65 characters, and their
  bodies are not wrapped. The commits of the owner were not changed.

